{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna","id":1527451,"title":"Let's chat legacy Fianna!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-25T21:16:58-08:00","id":1527451,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Let's chat legacy Fianna!","content":"I'm feeling a pretty solid grasp of many of the issues inherent in the old game, but one of the issues I'm still quite hazy on is the Fianna, and I'd love to hear some feedback and ideas about them. From my readings on them and catching whiffs of discourse regarding them, the following sticks out to me:<ul><li>Stereotyping them as the tribe of drunks, depicting an incredibly unhealthy stereotype of Irish culture, and romanticizing the Americanized 'fighting Irish' caricature of the culture i.e., Spirit Brew, Hangover Cure, et al.</li> <li>There are some rumblings that their tribe name may be problematic, but nothing definitive sticks out, and I'd like to learn more about this discourse and how important it is to Irish folk that the name change/stay the same.</li> <li>The unhealthy language that pertains to the objectification of their kinfolk, e.g., Guardians of the Caerns pg. 94:</li> </ul><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Merryck's comments: It's not without a certain sense of irony that the Fianna, self-avowed masters and mistresses of passion and abandon among the werewolves, despise the M***s. They believe that physical deformity shows a malevolence in the spirit as well. But at the same time, they're really into having wild, raucus parties, orgies if you ask my opinion. The Fianna dismiss any potential risk with this kind of activity their answer to slowing those driving passions is &quot;find a Kinfolk to slake your lust.&quot; How practical. Don't kid yourself; there are <i>many</i> M***s running around with red hair and green eyes, both in their tribe and outside it. </div> </div> </div>I THINK the original intent was to depict them as the parallel to dwarves in D&amp;D, but it only really manages to caricature unhealthy stereotypes. How do each of you approach these topics at your tables? If the Fianna were to get a redraft, how would you depict them? Are there more issues with the tribe I'm missing here? Also, how do you think they approach the relationship between Northern Ireland and the rest of the UK?<br /> <br /> I have some vague ideas on how to address this, but I am unsure if it's comprehensive enough or too heavy-handed:<ul><li>Reorient them away from the fighting/drunkard way they're written to recast them as storytellers and artisans of the Western Concordat.</li> <li>Drop the boozy powers entirely and replace them with something else, perhaps related to the way they recall past events, to play them up as storytellers.</li> <li>Further the meta by maybe altering the way they're written away from something that enables STs and players to avoid some of the more rapey/breeding aspects.</li> </ul>In short, I'd like this to be a thread to talk shop about the Fianna! What do you love, what do you hate, what causes headache or head-scratching at the tabletop, what is critical to hold onto in the meta, your favorite and least favorite NPCs, etc. Let's chat the red-furred Garou!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T12:59:55-08:00","id":1527512,"title":"","content":"The Fianna are one of my favorite tribes so I\u2019ll try to provide some help to the points you bring up and your questions. (Disclaimer: I must admit that as a younger person I was also fascinated by an imagined Irish culture that I was descended from; I listened to the Pogues religiously, I re-read \u2018Trinity\u2019 until the cover was falling off, I read all I could find about the supposed lineage of my surname, etc; all of this while being the fifth generation of my family born in the US. I cannot deny that this influenced my affection for the Fianna)<br /> <br /> \u2022The Fianna have definitely been given the treatment of an ethnic Irish stereotype in the US of rowdy drunks. If you go back on the forums you can find a thread from a now-gone (I believe) poster MyWifeIsScary which explored further exploring those ideas by making them the explicit lower-class/working-class footie hooligan tribe. Opinions varied. I\u2019ll have more to touch on this below but this description, which was clearly stereotypical and one could argue based in internalized stereotypes applied by an anti-Irish/anti-Catholic Victorian cultural attitude in both the US &amp; UK, further emphasized by the optional tribal weakness making it harder for the Fianna to resist temptation and indulgence across the board.<br /> <br /> \u2022The tribal name of \u2018Fianna\u2019 is less an issue of being problematic than being potentially limiting imo. Unlike the tribal names for Older Brother or Younger Brother, \u201cFianna\u201d does not have a cultural connotation that would make it taboo to invoke. Instead the issues surround the name are more pragmatic. For one it refers to an Irish legend of an ancient war-band; this in itself is not necessarily an issue, but it suggests a particularly Irish character which diverges from attempts to make the Fianna pan-Celtic/Gaelic. Now that being said, it\u2019s not unheard of for the Fianna or their equivalents to be invoked by non-Irish Gaelic-identified cultural media. The song \u2018the Men of Knoydart\u2019 has a good Scottish example of this. That said, in W5, the tribe name was an issue because that edition was explicitly trying to divorce the Garou tribes from real-world cultures, but kept the name Fianna which is explicitly Gaelic, if not necessarily explicitly Irish. Some alternates proposed for a more pan-Celtic tribal epithet have included W5\u2019s \u201cHart Warders\u201d as well as the \u201cHorned Singers\u201d or the more general \u201cChildren of Stag\u201d.<br /> <br /> \u2022The relationship between their Fianna and their kin is something that I think is one of the most interesting parts of the tribe and the tensions of their stated beliefs, their actions, their values, and contemporary values are rich fodder for drama. That said, of course, some groups may not want to explore these themes and by no means should they be obliged to, but as a game that describes itself as being for \u2018mature storytelling\u2019 in a \u2018gothic-punk world\u2019 I feel that it would be more of a loss to remove such elements. That said, they ought to be handled with care and attention, as with any other theme for a mature game.<br /> <br /> That said, moving onto your further ideas and points.<br /> <br /> \u2022Something like what you described has always been true, particularly as of the revised area. Of course the tribe in the past has maintained its Celtic connotations but the notion of the Fianna being the leading artisan and storytellers of the Garou Nation is well-established in canon; with some sources describing them as the originators of the Garou High Tongue and the first Klaives. That said, I do think further exploration of this theme could be beneficial. Explorations of the material culture and storytelling of the Nation in general with the Fianna as a lense for such discussion. Perhaps connect it to a further exploration of moots in general and the concept of the Silver Record and the Greater Litany (the oral tradition we are told surrounds the simplified tenets we get in the books).<br /> <br /> \u2022I\u2019ve got kind of a soft-spot for the booze related gifts but I wouldn\u2019t complain if they were made a Homid gift instead (I believe the Bone Gnawers also get the drinking gift iirc).<br /> <br /> \u2022I\u2019ve mentioned in a few places before on this forum that I\u2019ve come to imagine the Fianna and Fenrir as embodying a sort of yin-yang relation with each other as the tribes of Northern/Western Europe. The Fianna I see as being the tribe which explicitly upholds social bonds and the greater social life; they are the tribe most concerned with fertility, familial bonds, the story of the people as it relates to the life and history of the people. As the tribe most actively involved with their kinfolk and in tune with human customs as well as the relationships maintained with spiritual and Fey worlds. (With the Fenrir on the other hand being a more narrow, inwardly focused, death/war society who often live separately from their kin in order to uphold their obligations).<br /> <br /> \u2022My view on the geographical question is that I\u2019m perfectly content with saying that the Tribes of Stag and [War/Death Wolf] are not limited to particular regions on the European sub-continent although they may perhaps have particularly notable populations there alongside presence in other regions. Perhaps something like a slight crib from WtF to have both ideological/political Camps as well as geographical/cultural Lodges.<br /> <br /> \u2022While I can understand why a table may want to downplay certain themes of kinfolk with the Fianna, i personally wouldn\u2019t want to. While I think that accusations of exploitation writing (read this as something akin to the \u2018exploitation flick\u2019 genre of film) wrt the Fianna &amp; the Troubles has some merit to it, I do also think that it draws attention to themes that should be relevant for the Fianna and Werewolf in general. I think high-lighting the connections homid Garou have to the circumstances of their human kin-groups and how it affects their decision making is something worthwhile to explore. Furthermore, sectarian warfare is something while plentiful basis in human history and storytelling, I think extending it to homid Garou makes sense and I think that the Fianna are perhaps the tribe that exemplifies it best. <br /> <br /> This post has gone on fairly long so I\u2019ll leave it off here, though I do have more ideas on the subject, but I hope people find things in here that are interesting and I\u2019ll try to answer any questions folks may have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T13:49:22-08:00","id":1527514,"title":"","content":"The Fianna/Hart Warden reason for abusing Garou Born stems from one legend where a king without an arm was deemed unacceptable as a king due to his disability. However, I have seen people of Celtic nationality disagree with that.<br /> <br /> As for the name, as someone who doesn't speak English as her first language, the Fianna always stood out as the one you could never translate into your own language. In addition to the famous &quot;Fianna is just a word&quot; comment. Garou tribe names are in English, yes, but the implication is that they translate to local languages.<br /> <br /> In terms of redoing the tribe, I'd emphasise the Celts all around Europe and have aspects from them in the tribe as well. However, I don't mind that they are abusive towards the garou born or that they think the war of Rage was justified. We need tribes who are hypocrites and who fail to see the harm in their actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T15:27:06-08:00","id":1527520,"title":"","content":"The Revised Tribebook peppered its first chapter in names of subsidiary tribes that reflected their existence across Europe. Plenty of names to work with as replacements that aren't as uninspiring as Hart Wardens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T01:13:14-08:00","id":1527537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The relationship between their Fianna and their kin is something that I think is one of the most interesting parts of the tribe and the tensions of their stated beliefs, their actions, their values, and contemporary values are rich fodder for drama. That said, of course, some groups may not want to explore these themes and by no means should they be obliged to, but as a game that describes itself as being for \u2018mature storytelling\u2019 in a \u2018gothic-punk world\u2019 I feel that it would be more of a loss to remove such elements. That said, they ought to be handled with care and attention, as with any other theme for a mature game. </div> </div> </div>I am kinda mixed on this, but by and large, I do agree that holding on to some of the nuances in the problematic aspects can provoke good narratives and roleplay, and I want to more solidly highlight the aspects players are supposed to call out. I do wanna make clear I'm not seeking censorship for censorship's sake. I guess in this case I'm trying to create a representation that has the problems that are kept be ones that serve a narrative purpose, while not encouraging players to take the worst aspects of a tribe and see them as encouraged behavior or something to emulate, if that makes sense. That is, I don't wanna leave the moral ambiguity so ambiguous that it's read as an endorsement. I do think holding on to how destructive and hateful they can be of warborn garou provokes good roleplay, but I'm not entirely convinced about the 'grab a kinfolk and rape them' kinda aspects as being something to hold on to. But as you said, it calls for nuance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, I do think further exploration of this theme could be beneficial. Explorations of the material culture and storytelling of the Nation in general with the Fianna as a lense for such discussion. Perhaps connect it to a further exploration of moots in general and the concept of the Silver Record and the Greater Litany (the oral tradition we are told surrounds the simplified tenets we get in the books). </div> </div> </div>Some of the things that come to mind that might be able to take the place of some gifts could be perhaps taken from human-born gifts, like Apecraft's Blessing in place of resist toxin and Perfect Recall in place of Faerie Light. I could probably write up a reskinning of spirit brew that gives it more ambiguity, making it something that can be either drunk or consumed (I guess a WoD-flavored lembas bread to store gnosis for later). And like you said, the drinky-kinda gifts can be a more human-born affinity, rather than just a tribal one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My view on the geographical question is that I\u2019m perfectly content with saying that the Tribes of Stag and [War/Death Wolf] are not limited to particular regions on the European sub-continent although they may perhaps have particularly notable populations there alongside presence in other regions. Perhaps something like a slight crib from WtF to have both ideological/political Camps as well as geographical/cultural Lodges. </div> </div> </div>I admit I haven't read much into celtic history, but I do like the idea of representing them with a broader brush than just in Ireland.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Revised Tribebook peppered its first chapter in names of subsidiary tribes that reflected their existence across Europe. Plenty of names to work with as replacements that aren't as uninspiring as Hart Wardens. </div> </div> </div>Thank you for this. I've pulled some, and assembled a couple rough translations. I'm pretty fond of some of them:<ul><li><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Children of Stag</span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Keltoi</span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Celtae</span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Hounds of the Horned One</span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Skysingers</span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Night Claws</span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Fierce Ones</span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Damhra </span></span><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">(Herd of Stags</span></span><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">, personal favorite</span></span><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">)</span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Staig D\u2019amhr\u00e1n </span></span><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">(Stag</span></span><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">/informer</span></span><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">, part of a song</span></span><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. an informational singer</span></span><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">)</span></span></span></span></li> </ul>I'm partial to Skysingers if sticking to canon names. I'm a big fan of furthering the world meta, or more specifically, curating the experience, rather than retconning it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T01:34:50-08:00","id":1527540,"title":"","content":"As said above by Revised that rather than being solely Irish or even of the British Isles/Ireland the Fianna were well established as a Tribe that, in history, had enclaves all throughout the European continent but more importantly I think is that the Fianna in the modern world exist absolutely everywhere<br /> <br /> Whilst the Firehair Fianna certainly stand out as some of the more far flung there are Fianna everywhere that a European country imposed a colony.....which means honestly the Fianna should probably carry the most colonial baggage of all the Tribes.....but it also means that Latino, Sikh, Bangladeshi, Singaporean, Malay, Aboriginal, Pacific Islander, Nigerian, Yoruban etc. Garou all have a very good chance of being taken in by the Tribe of Stag. They should probably be one of the most diverse tribes culturally out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-29T13:56:55-08:00","id":1527608,"title":"","content":"I don't feel that this name is problematic, as from my conversations with a couple of Irish folks and what I have learned about Fion MacCumhil and the roving bands known as Fiana, they seem to fill the exact niche of wandering heroes the Garou Pack is bound to be. For me the major reason why Fianna is the well known name is because it's the dominant strain of the tribe that colonised the world, has significant cache in Europe and are the ones that got into the New World, Australia, Africa and the far East through accompanying their kinfolk and taking up opportunities to carve out their places outside the traditional strongholds of the Tribe.<br /> <br /> In practice, they would actually have quite a few localised factions based on Celtic ancestry throughout Iberia, France, Northern Italy and Western Germany who all felt the Fianna subtribe are selfaggrandazing assholes, but they all follow the same Totem and are part of the same nation even if they had conflicts at certain times.<br /> <br /> The fighting drunkard stereotype had mostly been fixed by Revised calling out the fact that earlier portrayals could look like really bad stereotypes of pop culture Irish. I do feel that there is an element here that should be kept, though. To me, a defining characteristic of the Fianna is passion. They are probably the most passionate tribe, driven by a desire to experience everything life has to offer and protect that which the Mother has left them. This means that they should be defined by a certain <i>joie de vivre</i>. They should be enjoying food, drink, company and sex. They should love the world and its inhabitants, enjoying every moment they spend indulging and defending the bounty they are given. This does not mean that they should be defined by excess, but I do feel that this can be played up without going into the whole Dennis Leary's worst Irish Drunkard.<br /> <br /> Another element to consider is that considering this <i>joie de vivre</i> of the Fianna they tend to adapt to the locals and their customs at a faster pace than others, creating offshoots trying to make a name for themselves beyond the identity of the settlers from the lands of the British Crown. &quot;Oh fuck you dad, Stag is fine, but Kirin is much better and you cannot stop me from pracicing Kailindo&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 12-29-2023, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-29T16:31:46-08:00","id":1527612,"title":"","content":"It's funny you mention, but I don't see the Fianna as having red hair, that might seem wrong, but I ended up having the standard appearance for Garou of a given tribe, transformed of course, like the Furies have black hair on top and white on the bottom, Shadow Lords they are completely black and with yellowish eyes, Stargazers are gray wolfs and so on. In the case of the Fianna, I always thought of them as having light brown fur, I don't know how to explain it. Leaving pseudo-stereotypes aside, what I'm going to say is more like a personal vision of the Fianna and what they could be, because for me they're not bad, despite being far from being saints, but so far I haven't seen any WOD creature that wasn't at least problematic in some way.<br /> <br /> As for the stereotype part, okay, I agree, but I wouldn't completely remove that part from alcohol, Fiannas like to enjoy life and this is one way of doing that and they have a craft beer that affect even garou, it's something that I think is really interesting (but only in games, in real life I don't even touch alcohol) and it makes sense, if it's really a problem, we can catch it take a little of your idea and expand it to arts, so they could use songs, dances as a way of telling stories and enjoying life at the same time, they would also have a predisposition to crafts and tell stories through paintings, composed music, poems and even tapestries and they would still use alcohol as something ritualistic in ceremonies and alternatively another drink could be used depending on the occasion such as herbal tea or fruit juice, (have something like that in the tribebook) however the use would be controlled, as improper use could lead to ruin, they would even have stories about heroes who lost themselves after falling deep into hedonism, including a problematic tribe with this theme, because every tribe has one or two of these (Except for GoF who achieved the feat of having three) it would even be cool and a lesson that, despite being beaten, is still relevant in my opinion.(In parallel I would think of versions of them in other cultures, you know Fiannas with oriental aesthetics or those who venerate la Santa de Los Muertos, that would be interesting, if this already exists I must have forgotten)<br /> <br /> As for objectifying kinfolk, I think the simplest thing would be to say that they are in favor of free love and even casual sex, and that's why it's normal for them to have frequent relationships with kinfolk and even with those outside of kinfolk. lineage, I know this is weird and more like my headcanon, but I see them like that, they just aren't shy about relationships, it's fun have someone like that in the group (mostly). Obviously there will be those who go beyond the limits, especially because being a Garou can open the door to problems with the Kinfolk that you should already know about.<br /> <br /> As for the problem with the Metis or Crinos, what I can think of is that they could see this as bad luck, but this varies depending on the Caern, like divergent opinions within the same tribe, but the parents will still be punished anyway. In this case I just think about ignoring that aspect until it can be relevant in some way, or they look at the born Crinos with shame because it's a mistake they made, it's not something I can reconcile actually, it's something that It exists and when it happens, we just deal with it the best way we can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-30T18:36:52-08:00","id":1527648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for objectifying kinfolk, I think the simplest thing would be to say that they are in favor of free love and even casual sex, and that's why it's normal for them to have frequent relationships with kinfolk and even with those outside of kinfolk. lineage, I know this is weird and more like my headcanon, but I see them like that, they just aren't shy about relationships, it's fun have someone like that in the group (mostly). </div> </div> </div>I have what, I think, is a pretty strong argument against this, and it's that the game offers no robust tabletop tools for navigating consent between the players and storytellers to gauge whether one is receptive to this or not. World of Darkness games on the whole aren't really built for it anyway, and it's important the horror is happening to characters and not players (traumatizing players is a good way to lose players IMO). While long-term tabletops with people who know each other well enough to navigate this can and will explore this of their own accord in a chronicle, I just don't think this is something that's a good idea to offer up in print as a turnkey 'yeah this tribe does this so you should too', especially since your average tabletop player is anything but equipped to navigate this kinda thing maturely without any safety tools to do so. It can be fun for mature players that make it a consensual experience, but I'm not sure it should be pushed as a social norm that's emblematic of the tribe. If it serves no narrative purpose, it's a lot more likely to generate groans and eye-rolls at the table, or turn people off from playing at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":27167,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","user":"mundusartis","date":". 12-30-2023, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-30T21:43:40-08:00","id":1527649,"title":"","content":"I always loved how passionate the Fianna were, but I tried to steer away from the tribe\u2019s more negative aspects. I have no problem with the name Fianna because it was the name of Fionn Mac Cumhail\u2019s war band, though I also don\u2019t mind Hart Wardens either (a hart is just an old word for a stag).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T17:58:15-08:00","id":1527965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for objectifying kinfolk, I think the simplest thing would be to say that they are in favor of free love and even casual sex, and that's why it's normal for them to have frequent relationships with kinfolk and even with those outside of kinfolk. lineage, I know this is weird and more like my headcanon, but I see them like that, they just aren't shy about relationships, it's fun have someone like that in the group (mostly). </div> </div> </div>I have what, I think, is a pretty strong argument against this, and it's that the game offers no robust tabletop tools for navigating consent between the players and storytellers to gauge whether one is receptive to this or not. World of Darkness games on the whole aren't really built for it anyway, and it's important the horror is happening to characters and not players (traumatizing players is a good way to lose players IMO). While long-term tabletops with people who know each other well enough to navigate this can and will explore this of their own accord in a chronicle, I just don't think this is something that's a good idea to offer up in print as a turnkey 'yeah this tribe does this so you should too', especially since your average tabletop player is anything but equipped to navigate this kinda thing maturely without any safety tools to do so. It can be fun for mature players that make it a consensual experience, but I'm not sure it should be pushed as a social norm that's emblematic of the tribe. If it serves no narrative purpose, it's a lot more likely to generate groans and eye-rolls at the table, or turn people off from playing at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T18:50:48-08:00","id":1527968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1527965#post1527965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have what, I think, is a pretty strong argument against this, and it's that the game offers no robust tabletop tools for navigating consent between the players and storytellers to gauge whether one is receptive to this or not. World of Darkness games on the whole aren't really built for it anyway, and it's important the horror is happening to characters and not players (traumatizing players is a good way to lose players IMO). While long-term tabletops with people who know each other well enough to navigate this can and will explore this of their own accord in a chronicle, I just don't think this is something that's a good idea to offer up in print as a turnkey 'yeah this tribe does this so you should too', especially since your average tabletop player is anything but equipped to navigate this kinda thing maturely without any safety tools to do so. It can be fun for mature players that make it a consensual experience, but I'm not sure it should be pushed as a social norm that's emblematic of the tribe. If it serves no narrative purpose, it's a lot more likely to generate groans and eye-rolls at the table, or turn people off from playing at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I'm experienced in this, but I've always believed that the characteristics of groups are more of a general rule, and as the name says, they don't represent the individual. That said, I think you could make a more puritan Fianna, a more nervous Child of Gaia, a more romantic GoF or a more sloppy Shadow Lord. I think that this structure of the tribe infers more from the environment in which it finds itself, as for relationships I agree, but I don't touch on that in the game so my opinion may not be worth much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T19:58:10-08:00","id":1527969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1527649#post1527649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always loved how passionate the Fianna were, but I tried to steer away from the tribe\u2019s more negative aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Along those lines, if the aforementioned negative aspects were omitted from something like an expanded quickstart sourcebook without ambiguous restriction (ie no scolding the reader while not actively encouraging it), would they still fundamentally be recognizable as the Fianna to you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that this structure of the tribe infers more from the environment in which it finds itself, as for relationships I agree, but I don't touch on that in the game so my opinion may not be worth much. </div> </div> </div>Sort of the same question as above for you as well. If one were to omit the bad things without embellishment (ie the stuff that enables tabletop sex pests or poorly caricaturing cultural stereotypes at the tabletop), and leave it to Storytellers to 'read between the lines' in terms of what they include in their stories (ie keep the passion and creativity), would they still be recognizable as Fianna to you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T21:12:40-08:00","id":1527974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1527969#post1527969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Along those lines, if the aforementioned negative aspects were omitted from something like an expanded quickstart sourcebook without ambiguous restriction (ie no scolding the reader while not actively encouraging it), would they still fundamentally be recognizable as the Fianna to you?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sort of the same question as above for you as well. If one were to omit the bad things without embellishment (ie the stuff that enables tabletop sex pests or poorly caricaturing cultural stereotypes at the tabletop), and leave it to Storytellers to 'read between the lines' in terms of what they include in their stories (ie keep the passion and creativity), would they still be recognizable as Fianna to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. They would still be recognizable as Fianna to me. And I agree that we need to discourage the kind of sexist, homophobic, transphobic and generally inappropriately sexual behavior that so often ruins games today. That\u2019s why I made it clear that I did not condone the negative aspects of the old Fianna stereotype. But yes, you can preserve the passion and creativity of Celtic culture in a new Fianna (Hart Warden) archetype without preserving the bad stuff.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T09:28:31-08:00","id":1528266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1527969#post1527969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Along those lines, if the aforementioned negative aspects were omitted from something like an expanded quickstart sourcebook without ambiguous restriction (ie no scolding the reader while not actively encouraging it), would they still fundamentally be recognizable as the Fianna to you?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sort of the same question as above for you as well. If one were to omit the bad things without embellishment (ie the stuff that enables tabletop sex pests or poorly caricaturing cultural stereotypes at the tabletop), and leave it to Storytellers to 'read between the lines' in terms of what they include in their stories (ie keep the passion and creativity), would they still be recognizable as Fianna to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe yes, maybe no, this is not unprecedented, there are even a GoF caern that seeks to heal and a CoG caern that are more fighters, that being said, maybe they don't look like their tribes at first glance, but that could make sense of Another perspective, other than that, there is the case of garou who are part of a tribe they don't want to belong to, but it's not like they have much choice. So yeah, maybe yes, maybe no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T09:31:27-08:00","id":1528267,"title":"","content":"Speaking of the Fianna's habits, they normally don't like Metis, but there is a mention that if one of them is born with servant horns he is seen as blessed by their spirit, how does that work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T09:45:44-08:00","id":1528268,"title":"","content":"I think they got rid of that in W5 (through the simple expedient of not having any more Crinos-born), and I for one am happy for that. I never liked the idea of having a whole tribe of heroes who were prejudiced against those who were born differently abled by an accident of birth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T12:29:16-08:00","id":1528278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1528268#post1528268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they got rid of that in W5 (through the simple expedient of not having any more Crinos-born), and I for one am happy for that. I never liked the idea of having a whole tribe of heroes who were prejudiced against those who were born differently abled by an accident of birth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I on the other hand consider it a sweeping under the rug of an important issue with an unspoken implication of 'this stuff is fine now, no need to interrogate it'.<br /> <br /> The Metis had problems, but I'd argue people's biggest problem is that they're uncomfortably realistic. Their portrayal can probably be toned down to reflect that things have gotten better and they need a new breed name (his about Crinos?), but if you're not comfortable with how they're treated that's the point.<br /> <br /> Then again I also have no issue with the Garou Nation being transphobic, but I understand that's divisive*. I probably support it more because I live on TERF Island, how nice it must be to live somewhere where the Left supports your existence...<br /> <br /> * As in nobody else likes it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T14:03:29-08:00","id":1528284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1528268#post1528268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they got rid of that in W5 (through the simple expedient of not having any more Crinos-born), and I for one am happy for that. I never liked the idea of having a whole tribe of heroes who were prejudiced against those who were born differently abled by an accident of birth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly, the Fianna are not the only tribe, they are just the worst, there are mentions of other tribes, but I would have to elaborate, secondly, I am not particularly bothered, just curious about how a metis with deer antlers was treated by the Fianna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T17:17:44-08:00","id":1528290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1528268#post1528268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they got rid of that in W5 (through the simple expedient of not having any more Crinos-born), and I for one am happy for that. I never liked the idea of having a whole tribe of heroes who were prejudiced against those who were born differently abled by an accident of birth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly I always thought this was about them being proud and unwilling to own up to their mistakes. Their attitude to life is bound to provide more metis than most other tribes, yet they have taken on a policy of ostracizing the child rather than the parents. It speaks to an interesting level of self delusion that can be played up for drama. Again, it shouldn't be the baseline, but it's a level of cognitive dissonance that's quite realistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-11T15:11:58-08:00","id":1528398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1528278#post1528278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I on the other hand consider it a sweeping under the rug of an important issue with an unspoken implication of 'this stuff is fine now, no need to interrogate it'.<br /> <br /> The Metis had problems, but I'd argue people's biggest problem is that they're uncomfortably realistic. Their portrayal can probably be toned down to reflect that things have gotten better and they need a new breed name (his about Crinos?), but if you're not comfortable with how they're treated that's the point.<br /> <br /> Then again I also have no issue with the Garou Nation being transphobic, but I understand that's divisive*. I probably support it more because I live on TERF Island, how nice it must be to live somewhere where the Left supports your existence...<br /> <br /> * As in nobody else likes it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I never really had a problem with the ugly side of garou society. Especially considering the other two of the big three were also pretty dubious.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T06:26:38-08:00","id":1529705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1528267#post1528267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of the Fianna's habits, they normally don't like Metis, but there is a mention that if one of them is born with servant horns he is seen as blessed by their spirit, how does that work?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d assume that ought to read \u2018antlers\u2019 based on Stag being patron spirit of the Tribe and a perceived connection to that patron trumping the instinctive Fianna dislike<br /> of being reminded that great passions can have ugly consequences (Something visible in their treatment of those whose birth breaches the Litany, as well as their tendency to emphasise the positive and forget the negative). <br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding the Fianna as a whole, I\u2019d say that their great charm is the ability to make being a Garou look FUN (In a way that only the Bone Gnawers come close to matching) and their great failing is a tendency to pursue the Joys of Living in a way that makes life harder for others (Sometimes for their own kinfolk, always for their rivals and all too often for their other neighbours). <br /> <br /> Also, one wrinkle in the fabric of their makeup that isn\u2019t always emphasised is that the Fianna aren\u2019t just werewolves, they\u2019re Fairy Tale werewolves: one element of 5th edition that I really enjoyed (Despite giving an actual groan at seeing the name for this tribe\u2019s successors) was the notion that the Hart Wardens more or less run on Fairy Tale logic (Especially when it comes to their rules of Hospitality).<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not going to lie, were one putting together a Hart Warden I would absolutely take Folkloric Tells as a flaw: it fits my conception of the Tribe quite beautifully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T14:05:06-07:00","id":1540468,"title":"","content":"I feel like there are some people here wouldn't really like how IRL wolves handle other wolves, especially puppies, with visible deformities or external signs of disease. I feel like part of the fun/horror is having Garou needing to deal with the compounded version of wolf aversion to new/different things combined with human tribalism/xenophobia. Literally being afflicted by instincts and spirit-pacts that would seek to compel you to act like a savage person and the whole of Garou Culture and Religion which seems to broadly indicate that such violence and intolerance is a good thing and 'if you don't like it, look what we're up against and tell us we're wrong for being violent and paranoid'. I think it is important in a horror game that the protagonists not be wholly righteous, and I think in that 90's feeling, even the 'good guys' should have detestable aspects that allow the PCs to be countercultural to their own side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","name":"Devidramoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27296_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T22:23:33-07:00","id":1540498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Devidramoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1540468#post1540468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like there are some people here wouldn't really like how IRL wolves handle other wolves, especially puppies, with visible deformities or external signs of disease. I feel like part of the fun/horror is having Garou needing to deal with the compounded version of wolf aversion to new/different things combined with human tribalism/xenophobia. Literally being afflicted by instincts and spirit-pacts that would seek to compel you to act like a savage person and the whole of Garou Culture and Religion which seems to broadly indicate that such violence and intolerance is a good thing and 'if you don't like it, look what we're up against and tell us we're wrong for being violent and paranoid'. I think it is important in a horror game that the protagonists not be wholly righteous, and I think in that 90's feeling, even the 'good guys' should have detestable aspects that allow the PCs to be countercultural to their own side.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the Fianna hate for deformities is not based on that. It is based on ONE Celtic myth about someone losing an arm and so being unable to be a king. That is what is referenced as the reason, not what wolves do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T00:46:51-07:00","id":1540501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Devidramoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1540468#post1540468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1540498#post1540498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> snip.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well regardless of the reason the OP's own HearthBound supplement doesn't paint the most flattering image of the tribe:<br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/IbX63Un.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/IbX63Un.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/IbX63Un.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> And it seems WtE version (now renamed Skysingers) is continuing this tradition:<br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/MgZcBXo.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/MgZcBXo.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/MgZcBXo.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> Of course this dosn't prevent the PC from focusing more on Fenna/Skysigner as lore keepers and musician not crinos hunters and kinfolk beaters...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T06:21:33-07:00","id":1540565,"title":"","content":"Wolves also don't have a habit of killing deformed pups--there's wolf populations where a pretty substantial percentage of the population have deformities (inbreeding is the culprit in the examples I'm aware of), and that wouldn't happen if the urban legends were accurate and wolves killed deformed pups. Most likely, this myth was spread by people who observed wolves eating pups who died of congenital issues and concluded that the wolf had killed them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T06:59:46-07:00","id":1540568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1540565#post1540565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolves also don't have a habit of killing deformed pups--there's wolf populations where a pretty substantial percentage of the population have deformities (inbreeding is the culprit in the examples I'm aware of), and that wouldn't happen if the urban legends were accurate and wolves killed deformed pups. Most likely, this myth was spread by people who observed wolves eating pups who died of congenital issues and concluded that the wolf had killed them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the assumption that nature is Cruel and there is no space for the disabled there.<br /> <br /> Ignoring that one eyed, lame legged and such wolves have thrived.<br /> <br /> I am curious what populations have deformities, though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T08:50:23-07:00","id":1540572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1540568#post1540568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or the assumption that nature is Cruel and there is no space for the disabled there.<br /> <br /> Ignoring that one eyed, lame legged and such wolves have thrived.<br /> <br /> I am curious what populations have deformities, though?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2009/04/090402171440.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Isle Royale's wolves</a>, and IIRC Scandinavia's too. A lot of them have malformed vertebrae, which sometimes causes partial paralysis. I guess I'm not really sure how visible it is externally, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T09:22:25-07:00","id":1540576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1540572#post1540572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2009/04/090402171440.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Isle Royale's wolves</a>, and IIRC Scandinavia's too. A lot of them have malformed vertebrae, which sometimes causes partial paralysis. I guess I'm not really sure how visible it is externally, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, that. There are also wolves here in Finland with atypical coats (one was dingo blonde!) that either indicate dog ancestry, or some goofy gene mutations due to inbreeding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T19:11:12-07:00","id":1540604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Devidramoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1540468#post1540468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like there are some people here wouldn't really like how IRL wolves handle other wolves, especially puppies, with visible deformities or external signs of disease. I feel like part of the fun/horror is having Garou needing to deal with the compounded version of wolf aversion to new/different things combined with human tribalism/xenophobia. Literally being afflicted by instincts and spirit-pacts that would seek to compel you to act like a savage person and the whole of Garou Culture and Religion which seems to broadly indicate that such violence and intolerance is a good thing and 'if you don't like it, look what we're up against and tell us we're wrong for being violent and paranoid'. I think it is important in a horror game that the protagonists not be wholly righteous, and I think in that 90's feeling, even the 'good guys' should have detestable aspects that allow the PCs to be countercultural to their own side.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only is the idea that wolves always kill the disabled among them wrong, as seen in the comments above, the Garou aren't affected by how wolves behave to begin with.<br /> <br /> They never were, and never will be. In fact, the irony of the Talons, as an example, is that while they preach natural purity, they're weirdos among wolves to the last, the same as every Wolf-Born.<br /> <br /> While there was some intent in the beginning of the game to have some of the Garou traditions and instincts to be a result of wolf instinct, the execution was based on lots of urban legends and outdated books.<br /> <br /> All in all, it is impossible for a bunch of humans playing a game to really grasp how real wolves think, and that's ok. Garou society, though, is from start to end based on how human societies work, and purely human prejudice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T20:56:40-07:00","id":1540605,"title":"","content":"While it's true that the wolf-influence among the Garou has always been riddled with errors, it's wrong to say that they have no basis in actual wolves. The greater influence of scent and howl culture are both based in actual wolf ethology. And it's as ridiculous to say that a bunch of humans will never grasp how wolves think as it is to say that members of one human group can't grasp how another human group thinks. This knowledge is imperfect, but I can't have perfect knowledge of what it's like to be French either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T00:44:45-07:00","id":1540611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1540605#post1540605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it's true that the wolf-influence among the Garou has always been riddled with errors, it's wrong to say that they have no basis in actual wolves. The greater influence of scent and howl culture are both based in actual wolf ethology. And it's as ridiculous to say that a bunch of humans will never grasp how wolves think as it is to say that members of one human group can't grasp how another human group thinks. This knowledge is imperfect, but I can't have perfect knowledge of what it's like to be French either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, even in Revised WtA was already pointing out the alpha myth was bunk. Tribebook Shadow Lords revised has a whole page dedicated to it and Storyteller's Guide revised makes mention of it as well.<br /> <br /> Plus, the more we study wolves, the more they resemble us. Disbanded wolves can come back to their home packs if they fail at starting their own pack, only 4 wolves in a hunt group ACTUALLY kill the prey (too scary for others) and wolves have different cultures from around the world. Yellowstone's culture is WILDLY different from that of British Columbia and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T10:51:59-07:00","id":1540637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1540605#post1540605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it's true that the wolf-influence among the Garou has always been riddled with errors, it's wrong to say that they have no basis in actual wolves. The greater influence of scent and howl culture are both based in actual wolf ethology. And it's as ridiculous to say that a bunch of humans will never grasp how wolves think as it is to say that members of one human group can't grasp how another human group thinks. This knowledge is imperfect, but I can't have perfect knowledge of what it's like to be French either.</div> </div> </div> </div>The influence of scent and howl comes from the interpretation about those made by game developers that only had secondary accounts of the phenomena and no academic study on the matter.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar110_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"110\" data-vbnamecard=\"110\">Ana Mizuki</a> said the important parts, but I want to add and explain. I'm not saying that to understand wolves is impossible. I'm saying that expecting this from a bunch of gamers is ridiculous. And I stand for this.<br /> <br /> It means to expect that both the developers of the game have an incredible degree of understanding about how a wolf think and behave, that the game books make a pristine work at transmitting this understanding, and that the average player deeply incorporates such knowledge.<br /> <br /> Sorry, but that's simply ridiculous. So much so that the more you actually studies about RL wolves with academic material up to date, the more you see how much the game got simply everything wrong.<br /> <br /> Literally everything the Garou do and point to wolves to justify themselves is actually not how wolves behave at all, but instead how many human societies did things through history, and many humans today want to behave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T11:31:29-07:00","id":1540640,"title":"","content":"Just to add to this, Ways of the Wolf had a lot of good info but also a lot it got very, very wrong. But more importantly is it also tells a little bit too much on some topics that don't add a ton to playability of lupus. The advisors they had on the book were part of a club that would catch wolf pups in the woods to be bred or sold as pets. With the information they do give on dens and behavior around dens, one could themselves use that info to steal a wolf pup if they were so inclined. I've had to do a lot of rewriting on the breed to undo some of that TMI in addition to undoing the toxic projection of masculine stereotypes on the breed and pack structures.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T12:26:25-07:00","id":1540646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1540637#post1540637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It means to expect that both the developers of the game have an incredible degree of understanding about how a wolf think and behave, that the game books make a pristine work at transmitting this understanding, and that the average player deeply incorporates such knowledge.<br /> <br /> Sorry, but that's simply ridiculous. So much so that the more you actually studies about RL wolves with academic material up to date, the more you see how much the game got simply everything wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the end of the day, even if this is a horror game trying to be serious, I'd just say depict wolves like characters in xenofiction. Because that way you do not lose the close ties to wolves but also don't make it too complicated for players.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T12:46:35-07:00","id":1540647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1540640#post1540640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to add to this, Ways of the Wolf had a lot of good info but also a lot it got very, very wrong. But more importantly is it also tells a little bit too much on some topics that don't add a ton to playability of lupus. The advisors they had on the book were part of a club that would catch wolf pups in the woods to be bred or sold as pets. With the information they do give on dens and behavior around dens, one could themselves use that info to steal a wolf pup if they were so inclined. I've had to do a lot of rewriting on the breed to undo some of that TMI in addition to undoing the toxic projection of masculine stereotypes on the breed and pack structures.<br /> \u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>.....They what now?<br /> <br /> Speaking of toxic projection, to me it is not the alpha that is the worst toxic stereotype. It is the omega, it is the idea that someone MUST be the lowest and someone MUST be the scapegoat. Because there can be a leader with no abuse, but the concept of omega needs abuse to exist.<br /> <br /> Which dovetails nicely into Legacy Fianna. The way they make a spectacle out of the crinos-born in a way that is creepy is very telling. Because nothing stops the tribe from just not accepting them, instead the Fianna intentionally keep some crinos-born around to serve as scapegoats and warnings for young garou. That to me has always been extremely twisted and very much leaning into the dominance myth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T16:06:48-07:00","id":1540661,"title":"","content":"Though, Omega-verse fiction is quickly knocking that setup just a bit off course and into D/s territory. Hopefully, the greek ordinal terms for wolf packs will be considered too close to slash to use in any other context and we'll be free of them on the werewolf end.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm an alpha!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, my!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No! A tough guy! A real dominant man!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;OH, MY!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T16:10:43-07:00","id":1540662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1540647#post1540647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> .....They what now?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>pg. 13:<br /> <br /> <img width=\"262\" height=\"267\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/W3047wr.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/W3047wr.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/W3047wr.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> I'm sure they meant well, but...goodness has a lot of this book aged like milk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T18:31:32-07:00","id":1540677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1540662#post1540662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> pg. 13:<br /> <br /> <img width=\"262\" height=\"267\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/W3047wr.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/W3047wr.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/W3047wr.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> I'm sure they meant well, but...goodness has a lot of this book aged like milk.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... Interesting.<br /> <br /> And disturbing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T23:50:35-07:00","id":1540692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1540661#post1540661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, Omega-verse fiction is quickly knocking that setup just a bit off course and into D/s territory. Hopefully, the greek ordinal terms for wolf packs will be considered too close to slash to use in any other context and we'll be free of them on the werewolf end.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm an alpha!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, my!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No! A tough guy! A real dominant man!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;OH, MY!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>With W5 allowing garouxgarou pairings to result in fertile offspring, we can now insert ABO into it fully XD<br /> <br /> It might sound weird but there is quite a bit of societal commentary on the dynamics.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1540662#post1540662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> pg. 13:<br /> <br /> <img width=\"262\" height=\"267\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/W3047wr.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/W3047wr.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/W3047wr.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> I'm sure they meant well, but...goodness has a lot of this book aged like milk.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel a lot of wolf stuff has, but man the devs should have thought about the sources. ESPECIALLY as WtA is veeeery critical of captive born garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T23:59:53-07:00","id":1540753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1540692#post1540692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With W5 allowing garouxgarou pairings to result in fertile offspring, we can now insert ABO into it fully XD<br /> <br /> It might sound weird but there is quite a bit of societal commentary on the dynamics.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... does everyone finds the Gnawers submissive and breedable, then, or is it by some other metric?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel a lot of wolf stuff has, but man the devs should have thought about the sources. ESPECIALLY as WtA is veeeery critical of captive born garou. </div> </div> </div>I wonder if it was something that they found out about during the later run of the game, and subsequently shifted away from for obvious reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T00:45:31-07:00","id":1540754,"title":"","content":"Query? ABO?<br /> <br /> Cos that's really not a nice word here in Oz....but I figure it means something else elsewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T00:46:41-07:00","id":1540755,"title":"","content":"Ah! Brain worked it out. Alpha/Beta/Omega?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T07:58:33-07:00","id":1540770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1540753#post1540753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... does everyone finds the Gnawers submissive and breedable, then, or is it by some other metric?</div> </div> </div> </div>.... Fuck it, in for a penny in for a pound, YES.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1540753#post1540753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if it was something that they found out about during the later run of the game, and subsequently shifted away from for obvious reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they ever really made it a big deal. So Gnawers and Walkers might look dog-ish, but not dog-like. I am pretty sure they had no idea of coywolves, because Nuwisha would have included that in its design.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers revised DID make it clear you have to be VERY high content to become a garou, so that took out a lot of Clement Lupus potentials (but not the labwolf nor the poodlewolf, funny enough.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T09:31:41-07:00","id":1540783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1540770#post1540770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> .... Fuck it, in for a penny in for a pound, YES.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it beats being reheated Nosferatu-but-Garou...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think they ever really made it a big deal. So Gnawers and Walkers might look dog-ish, but not dog-like. I am pretty sure they had no idea of coywolves, because Nuwisha would have included that in its design.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers revised DID make it clear you have to be VERY high content to become a garou, so that took out a lot of Clement Lupus potentials (but not the labwolf nor the poodlewolf, funny enough.) </div> </div> </div>I meant more in a sense of realizing what was going on IRL, but we did get the &quot;werewolves not dogs&quot; rather loudly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T23:44:36-07:00","id":1540879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527451-let-s-chat-legacy-fianna?p=1540770#post1540770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't think they ever really made it a big deal. So Gnawers and Walkers might look dog-ish, but not dog-like. I am pretty sure they had no idea of coywolves, because Nuwisha would have included that in its design.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny enough I actually rember reading a homebrew setting that features coywolves, Granted it's implied that they only recently came into existence long after the other fera's genocide the garou in this setting version of the war of rage...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T14:01:24-07:00","id":1541081,"title":"","content":"As a non irish Celt i felt that revised was doing it correct by writting them as the Celtic tribe rather than the american steriotypes on the irish tribe.<br /> the name makes sense in term of in clan politics as ireland is the only independant celtic nation and the large irish american presence.<br /> Going forward id have really liked to have seen the other celtic groups developed, especially the brittany and cornish peoples maybe even flirting with niche presences in spain and italy and discuss broadening demograpics in a cosmepolitan world eg people like jamaican irish manager whose very very fianna<br /> <br /> With that in mind i dislike the hart wardens and find them subtly offensive in a way which is hard to articulate and pin down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-27-2024, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-29T10:32:37-07:00","id":1541201,"title":"","content":"I didn't read the whole thread but this is our approach for Fianna.<br /> <br /> Fianna are an everpresent tribe in our games, since we are from north italy, and north italy is Gallia Cisalpina. Even genetically, north italians has a lot of gaulish ancestry, and despite in the books italian fianna are quoted only one time when they defeated Rome in its prime, we decided to make them one of the most present tribe in our lands and story. People from modern day Veneto suffer the SAME stereotypes of irish people. They are truly lookalike.<br /> <br /> We did with the Fianna what we did with every tribe : a tribe of werewolves its their own culture, they are of course tied to human cultures, but *werewolf tribe*=*that human culture* it's not a correct equation. Fianna does not equals Irish People, but of course, they could do it. Wendigo does not equals indigenous northern pepole (just think about their totem...) but they can. Same with the Fenris. I don't know a single german or scandinavian strength-hardliner who also thinks good things about a literall demon (Fenris). We like our game very dark and street level,so we try to look at the core of every tribe. Fianna are storytellers, champions of traditions, territorial conservatives, but also life-lovers, defenders of rural areas very connected to their roots as werewolves but also in a human way. For us they also embody Stag as the embodiment of the hunt. Here in north italy, one of our most famous legend is the Wild Hunt. Our fianna are relentless predators and hunters that revel after a bloody hunt against a wyrm spawn or whatever was the target.<br /> <br /> In short terms, we try to see the core of the tribe, understanding how we can adapt it to our setting, realizing that a tribal werewolf culture is not the product of a human culture, but a mirror of the people from where the tribe originated. But it's fucking 2024 guys. If a player or a storyteller want to play a Fianna without falling in the Irish Celtic stereotype he should be free to do so, focusing on what the fianna are at their heart, what stag symbolize, and why that cub ended up in the fianna accepted by the totem. Same with the other tribes, especially the tribes with demons and mythological creatures as totems.<br /> <br /> After they putted Wendigo running a sept in Africa , and opening many tribes far more, I realized this game can be personalized (respecting the canon) far more than it seems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 08-30-2024, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}